   "evidence": "Chart.lean:124 `{n : \u2115\u221e\u03c9} [ENat.LEInfty n]`; Chart.lean:156-157 `theorem exists_norm_chartZeroOrder_apply_le ... (hDs : ContMDiffCovariantDerivativeOn F n D univ)`. The proof bounds the continuous `chartZeroOrder` on a compact closure. The Mathlib class at CovariantDerivative/Basic.lean:108 has no lemma for lowering `k`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/CauchyRiemann/ZeroCount.lean",
   "fix": "Add `{n : \u2115\u221e\u03c9} [ENat.LEInfty n]` to the section variables and use `(hDs : ContMDiffCovariantDerivativeOn \u2102 n D univ)`. All six theorems that include `hDs` then hold for any smoothness level, including C\u2070.",
   "issue": "`hDs : ContMDiffCovariantDerivativeOn \u2102 \u221e D univ` is stronger than used. Its only consumer, `FiniteBundleAtlas.exists_norm_chartZeroOrder_apply_le`, takes any `{n : \u2115\u221e\u03c9} [ENat.LEInfty n]` and only needs the zeroth-order term to be continuous. Mathlib has no lemma for lowering the smoothness index of this class, so callers with a C^k operator cannot weaken their hypothesis to fit.",
   "line": 94
  }
